     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That's twice the usual maximum.\n- The maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg, with a maximum of about 850\u20131,000 mg per dose when given three times daily.\n- Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I can then enter it exactly as written. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
